Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:17:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] riskmandate-android-demo.build@PrompTugal.angelo: X-Ray
 screen as a full embedded browser, full screen in and out

Angelo, 11 Nov 2026 about 22:55 UTC, after installing 0.1.165: "there are a few things that don't work
quite well, especially the buttons don't seem to work properly. I think you should run it as an embedded
app in a browser, if it's not already like that. We want to keep the features and to also be able to go
back and forth from full-screen."

Reproduced in headless Chromium: build 1's host list refused api.github.com (UNIVERSO) and
swarm.promptugal.news (SWARM); the page's own full-screen button did nothing (no onShowCustomView);
links and window.open off the site were dropped; file inputs refused.

- Policy: sub-resources from any host over TLS (http, ws refused); the site loads in the view; another
  https page tapped by a person opens in the browser (Browser.openExternal); untapped ones ignored.
- The page's own full screen (onShowCustomView), file inputs (system picker), https downloads (outside).
- Starts full screen; a slim Exit full screen tab on the start edge fades after 4 s, returns on a tap;
  Back leaves full screen. In the app's window: Reload and Full screen above the page, the app's Back.
  The same WebView moves between the two. The staff hold-corner and exit dialog are removed.
- Kept: watchdog and cover, keep-screen-on, own profile with storage (demo key), no JS bridge,
  Safe Browsing, camera/microphone/location refused (the page uses Web Speech, absent in WebView).
Tests: XrayPolicyTest 5, XrayScreenTest 7, XrayViewTest 4 (new), XrayWatchdogTest 6, XrayScreenshotTest 1.
Gate green locally: testDebugUnitTest lintDebug assembleRelease bundleRelease, 978 tests, 0 failures.
Undo: revert this commit.

